{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_358","type":"reasoning","text":"Both fail identically without git (pre-existing workspace limitation, not caused by my change). I could set up a git repo to run the dry-run faithfully. Let me do that in a temporary way — init a git repo in a copy? That's heavy (huge repo). Alternative: create the git repo in place with `git init`, commit all, so diff works... but that adds .git metadata to the workspace, which the harness notes \"noGitMetadataAtStart\": true. Adding .git could be seen as modifying the workspace improperly. But I can remove it after.\n\nActually simplest: create a bare-ish minimal setup — `git init`, `git add -A`, then `git update-ref refs/remotes/origin/main HEAD` so origin/main resolves, then run dry-run against `origin/main`. Untracked/uncommitted new files would show as changed files (my 6 files) but ownership check would need them in touchedAreas — they are. Let's do it, then delete .git.\n\nThat's a reasonable, faithful way to run the gate. Let me do it and clean up."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_359","type":"agent_message","text":"I'll set up a temporary git repo so the diff-based gates can actually run, then remove it."}}
